# Q through the actual fixed-MTU DeltaSerializer

The **fixed-caller resource subgate passes** for the frozen 30-cell table on GNU
Rust 1.94. Q matches B's logical/physical Rust and native C allocation fields and
buffer capacities, while preserving all B/P/Q decisions and full wire bytes.
The [general component gate](chitchat-stateful-result-20261029.md) stays negative;
neither result replaces the other. Q is not adopted in Root, and CPU/RSS,
MSRV/Windows, package distribution and full release/host gates remain open.

## Exact scope and premeasurement corrections

This binds real DeltaSerializer::with_mtu, node/KV/max-version/DeltaBuilder work,
finish, final Delta::serialize_to_vec and destruction in one region. The final
serialization's second compression pass remains included. The driver uses the
documented API contract: one fixed MTU and stop at first false. It does not
substitute a Blob writer, force a cache branch, or claim complete ClusterState/
network/public-consumer coverage. In particular, compute_delta's ignored
max-version-false return is not modeled as an extra subsequent node attempt.

The table has MTUs 100/198/1000/16384/40000/65507 and five sequence families:
small distinct KVs; large then small; small then boundary; rejecting boundary;
and multiple nodes with max-version on empty nodes. Every key, value, node ID,
port/version, payload seed `0x0741028` and request order is frozen. Only the actual
constructor selects its threshold. A declared trailing request after rejection
must not execute. This finite ASCII95/repeat table is not all possible input data.

Two fixture errors were corrected **before any performance cohort**, without
changing Q, any runtime method, numerical MTU/payload boundary or release threshold:

1. Initial table `abe9b000...` used longer node-a/large identities with a value
   length borrowed from the original node/k corpus. Whole-source scalar-length
   review found the intended large-admission old floor was MTU+4. The initial
   B compiler/source/object context is retained; no controls/cohort executed.
   Separate r1 restores original node/k identities, giving floor MTU-2, and
   requires actual large admission/ambiguous-branch coverage before observation.
2. The first r1 B semantic control refuses the original final-serialization
   assert: actual 50 versus stored 60. Its max-version-after-KV sequence violates
   NodeDelta's canonical invariant. Source review confirms compute_delta emits
   max-version only for an empty node. Keep the assert and first failure; r2 fixes
   only this input family, with an independent canonical-order preflight before
   preparation. All r1 B/P/Q builds and the first B refusal remain; no r1 P/Q
   controls or cohort ran.

Accepted r2 table SHA-256:
`4a3308a82d014fb58df808a9f3984922537a80c02219610cdf5ee6fa1ec4a1f9`.
Each actual image must pass original allocator/C/tag/239-wire and generic
